Subject: Drop the unused NAMESPACE variable

Why: find-scale-down-blockers.sh sets NAMESPACE but never reads it (the -n flag works through NS_FLAG), which shellcheck reports as SC2034 now that make shellcheck lints the gke-* skills. The patch drops the two dead lines; the script behaves the same.
Local-Issue: none (#2867)
Upstream-Issue: none filed yet
Retire-When: upstream drops or uses the NAMESPACE variable

diff --git a/assets/find-scale-down-blockers.sh b/assets/find-scale-down-blockers.sh
--- a/assets/find-scale-down-blockers.sh
+++ b/assets/find-scale-down-blockers.sh
@@ -35,12 +35,10 @@ EOF
 }
 
 NS_FLAG=(-A)
-NAMESPACE=""
 while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
   case "$1" in
     -h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
     -n)        [[ -z "${2:-}" ]] && { echo "Error: -n requires a namespace." >&2; exit 1; }
-               NAMESPACE="$2"
                NS_FLAG=(-n "$2"); shift 2 ;;
     *)         echo "Unknown arg: $1" >&2; usage; exit 1 ;;
   esac
